Fixes to the Objective-C reader of lizard 1.26.1.

- It shares the C and C++ fixes in clike and clike_states: raw strings, digit
  separators, preprocessor conditionals, templates and parameter lists.
- A block literal at file scope, `^(int v) { ... }`, is no function named
  `(`.
- A C or C++ function in an Objective-C file keeps the C rules: the selector
  rules read `override` or `try` as a name.
- An attribute macro after a selector, `NS_SWIFT_NAME(sw(x:))` or
  `NS_AVAILABLE(10_0)`, no longer renames the method `)` or adds a parameter.
- Each selector part counts as one parameter.

